lse,"num_turns":36,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the DocService verdict to `.theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-docservice.md` and committed it as `2d578c0`. That is the only file changed. Both acceptance commands pass. `theseus validate` reports one expected warning: rule D3 wants a second diagnosis from another model family, and that is still to come.\n\n## Verdict\n**Migrate the small, self-contained modules to TypeScript, and keep the core as it is for now.** The verdict is conditional on wave 0 finishing first. Confidence is medium; agreement is `partial` until the second diagnosis.\n\n| Part | Decision |\n|---|---|\n| `utilsDocService`, `wopiUtils`, `editorDataMemory` | Migrate. `utilsDocService` already has 18 tests; the other two get characterization tests first. |\n| `DocsCoServer`, `canvasservice`, `converterservice`, `wopiClient` (about 8,900 lines) | Keep. Add characterization tests only, then reassess after wave 1. |\n| `database.js` | Retire. It can never load: it needs `mongodb`, which is in no `package.json`, and `./config.json`, which does not exist. |\n| Database connectors, RabbitMQ, entry scripts | Keep. |\n\nThe weighted matrix scores 3.10 out of 5, which would suggest migrating everything. I went against it for the core, and the file says why:\n- **No tests:** the core has none, so rule D1 blocks changing it.\n- **Hard to untangle:** seven modules require `DocsCoServer`, and it requires several of them back. About 2,500 lines of `install` are closures that cannot be tested on their own.\n- **Little gain:** converting the core as it stands would mostly add `any` types and pull the fork away from upstream.\n\n## Packet plan (8 packets, P1 to P8)\n- **Wave 0:**\n  - Characterization tests for `wopiUtils`, `editorDataMemory` and the exported helpers of `DocsCoServer`.\n  - An interop packet that adds the TypeScript toolchain and converts `utilsDocService` as the worked example.\n- **Wave 1:**\n  - Convert `wopiUtils` and `editorDataMemory`.\n  - Investigate and remove `database.js`.\n  - Investigate which `install` closures could be pulled out safely, and how often upstream changes these files. That result feeds the reassessment of the core.\n\n## Lessons for the Atlas\nI'm leaving these here because this run was not allowed to edit the packet, the card or the scoreboard.\n- **Card corrections:**\n  - `database.js` is dead code, not an open question.\n  - `pkg.scripts` in `DocService/package.json` lists `editorDataRedis.js`, which is not in the repo.\n  - `DocsCoServer.js:155` has a latent bug: when a backend has no `EditorStat`, it falls back to `new editorDataStorage()`. It cannot trigger with the bundled backend today.\n- **Churn data is useless here.** The fork has a single import commit, so `churn_90d` will stay meaningless until we look at upstream history.\n- **Shared toolchain.** The TypeScript setup is repo-wide. If the Common diagnosis also plans an interop packet, `SUMMARY.md` should keep only one.\n- **Method friction, not recorded.** I did not append to `friction.jsonl`. `AGENTS.md` requires it, but this run's rules and the one-file budget forbid it. Three things to log there:\n  - The two rule sets contradict each other.\n  - The spec never says whether \"high score\" means \"favors change\" for coupling and oracle strength.\n  - The `wave` field is unclear when the first packets are wave 0 but the migrations are wave 1. I set `wave: 1`.","ttft_ms":1422,"type":"result","duration_ms":175499,"uuid":"2401bedc-9e35-4115-9e74-78ec8eb1b2db","ttft_stream_ms":962,"time_to_request_ms":340,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":198,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":33,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":6,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":14,